# PDF Builder — the console's sign-in, session and sign-out, by hand.
# VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension, then click "Send Request" above any block.
# Rider and Visual Studio open .http files natively.
#
# The console does all of this itself; these requests show what it sends. @adminKey is the published,
# local-only key that compose.yaml is configured with: it works against `docker compose up` and nowhere
# else. Set @host to 8080 when running under Docker.
#
# The session cookie is Secure. Clients that follow browser rules will not send it over plain HTTP to
# anything but localhost.

@host = http://localhost:5052
@adminKey = adm_lPQ25ykvuTW7HdOJLaJzfqnJsT4cKQfwwR5pgq4o


### Sign in — 204 and Set-Cookie: blocks.pdf.console=…; HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Strict.
# Without X-Console: 1 the answer is 403 CONSOLE_HEADER_REQUIRED. A wrong key is 401 AUTH_INVALID_KEY;
# the sixth failure in a minute from one address is 429 RATE_LIMITED.
POST {{host}}/api/console/session
X-Console: 1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "adminKey": "{{adminKey}}" }


### When the session ends — 200 { "expiresAt": … }. The admin key in X-Api-Key is not a session: 401.
GET {{host}}/api/console/session


### A change made with the session must carry X-Console: 1 — this one does.
POST {{host}}/api/admin/clients
X-Console: 1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "ecommerce", "name": "E-commerce" }


### The same change without the header — 403 CONSOLE_HEADER_REQUIRED, nothing is created.
POST {{host}}/api/admin/clients
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "erp", "name": "ERP" }


### Acting as a client: X-Client-Id is honoured for the operator only (the session or the admin key).
GET {{host}}/api/templates
X-Client-Id: ecommerce


### The permissions a key can be given, with what each allows.
GET {{host}}/api/admin/scopes


### Sign out — 204; the cookie is cleared and a copy of it is refused on every instance from now on.
DELETE {{host}}/api/console/session
X-Console: 1
